_🧹 Nitpick_ | _🔵 Trivial_

**Consider using a more robust query for the input element.**

The `getByPlaceholderText('')` works but is fragile—it depends on the implementation detail that the placeholder becomes empty when tags exist. Using `getByRole('textbox')` would be more resilient to implementation changes.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested improvement</summary>

```diff
   it('respects maxTags limit', () => {
     render(<TagInputWrapper maxTags={2} initialTags={['One', 'Two']} />);
-    const input = screen.getByPlaceholderText('');
+    const input = screen.getByRole('textbox');

     // Attempt to add third tag
     fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'Three' } });
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  it('respects maxTags limit', () => {
    render(<TagInputWrapper maxTags={2} initialTags={['One', 'Two']} />);
    const input = screen.getByRole('textbox');

    // Attempt to add third tag
    fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'Three' } });
    fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Enter', code: 'Enter' });

    expect(screen.queryByText('Three')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  });
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

