_🧹 Nitpick_ | _🔵 Trivial_

**Good accessibility test coverage.**

The live region test properly verifies screen reader announcements. Consider cleaning up the verbose inline comments (lines 77-80) and adding tests for additional scenarios:

- Backspace key removal of last tag
- Duplicate tag announcement (`"Tag is already added"`)
- Max tags reached announcement (`"Cannot add more than X tags"`)



<details>
<summary>💡 Example tests for additional scenarios</summary>

```tsx
it('removes last tag via Backspace on empty input', () => {
  render(<TagInputWrapper initialTags={['First', 'Last']} />);
  const input = screen.getByRole('textbox');

  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Backspace', code: 'Backspace' });

  expect(screen.queryByText('Last')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText('First')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

it('announces when duplicate tag is attempted', () => {
  render(<TagInputWrapper initialTags={['Existing']} />);
  const input = screen.getByRole('textbox');

  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'Existing' } });
  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Enter', code: 'Enter' });

  const liveRegion = screen.getByRole('status', { hidden: true });
  expect(liveRegion).toHaveTextContent('Tag "Existing" is already added');
});
```
</details>

